* The following JavaScript code uses a for loop to print the Fibonacci sequence. It initializes two variables and updates them each iteration to generate the next number in the sequence.
* This loop continues as long as the current number is less than 256. It therefore stops before printing 256 and prints all preceding numbers in the sequence.

```javascript
let a = 0;
let b = 1;
for (let i = 0; a < 256; i++) {
    console.log(a);
    let next = a + b;
    a = b;
    b = next;
}
```
